ic:editor","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2025-03-02T23:06:07Z","updated_at":"2025-03-03T00:10:55Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.4.rc3.official [15ff45068]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.rc3 - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - GeForce GTX 780M - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-4700HQ CPU @ 2.40GHz (8 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nConverting a project give absolutely NO feedback at all if it's a success or a failure, neither the output to console which is at least known (by the process ?) is displayed.\n\nDon't know why @KoBeWi claims:\n\n> we could easily display converter's output, but not the errors that appear in the console.\n\nThat's would be quite a shame to have a process give output and won't be able to keep it or reuse it for other purpose. There is room here for improvement and maybe better inter-process communication and/or handling.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nConvert a Godot 3 project and witness nothing is reported to you, success or failure... you don't know what happened after potential conversion.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nA project reference is given in #102050","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103487/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103487/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}